From 02a738d2a3fd0c01abfeb33bbdb0518c10475653 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alex Lopes Pereira <noreply@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 1 Aug 2026 00:24:35 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] feat(brief): flag --vm para briefs no-mistakes dentro da
 microVM
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Duas diferencas em relacao ao host, e so essas duas.

Regra 7: a proibicao de mexer no daemon continua, mas o motivo passa a ser
verdadeiro no contexto. Na VM o daemon e do proprio crewmate, nao uma
instancia compartilhada — reinicia-lo nao machuca outras lanes, destroi o
run dele. Regra cuja razao declarada e falsa e regra que agente aprende a
descontar.

Linha final: na VM o crewmate faz o merge (squash + apaga a branch,
tolerando "already merged") e reporta done: PR {url} merged. A microVM e
destruida no fim do run, entao um PR parado em CI-verde nao teria quem o
mergeasse. Casa com a metodologia do capitao — ele confere o resultado,
nao o merge.

O caminho do host sai byte a byte identico ao anterior (regra 7 e linha
final comparadas contra o brief do nm-cpf-1, gerado antes da mudanca).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018QWb2syf9uXhfQzzDkt8rx
---
 bin/fm-brief.sh | 40 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 36 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/bin/fm-brief.sh b/bin/fm-brief.sh
index 9c98723..7d218cc 100755
--- a/bin/fm-brief.sh
+++ b/bin/fm-brief.sh
@@ -21,6 +21,10 @@
 #   omitting both still fails loudly so an accidental omission is never silent.
 #   Set FM_SECONDMATE_CHARTER='<charter>' to fill the charter text.
 #   Set FM_SECONDMATE_SCOPE='<scope>' to write a routing scope distinct from the charter text.
+#   --vm says the crewmate runs inside a shuru microVM. It changes two things in a
+#   no-mistakes brief: the daemon is the VM's own (not the host's shared instance),
+#   and the crewmate merges its own PR after CI is green, because the VM is torn
+#   down at the end of the run and nothing would be left to merge it.
 #   --herdr-lab is mandatory when the task will issue Herdr lifecycle commands.
 #   It adds the hard isolation contract backed by bin/fm-herdr-lab.sh.
 #   The flag must be explicit because {TASK} is filled after scaffolding and the
@@ -94,12 +98,16 @@ fi
 KIND=ship
 HERDR_LAB=0
 NO_PROJECTS=0
+# --vm: the crewmate runs inside a shuru microVM, where the no-mistakes daemon is
+# the VM's own (born at boot, dies with it) instead of the host's shared one.
+VM=0
 POS=()
 for a in "$@"; do
   case "$a" in
     --scout) KIND=scout ;;
     --secondmate) KIND=secondmate ;;
     --herdr-lab) HERDR_LAB=1 ;;
+    --vm) VM=1 ;;
     --no-projects) NO_PROJECTS=1 ;;
     *) POS+=("$a") ;;
   esac
@@ -302,6 +310,32 @@ read -r MODE _ <<EOF
 $("$FM_ROOT/bin/fm-project-mode.sh" "$REPO")
 EOF
 
+# Rule 7 and the no-mistakes finish line both hinge on WHERE the daemon lives.
+# On the host it is one shared instance and restarting it kills other lanes'
+# in-flight runs. Inside a shuru microVM it is that VM's own daemon, started by
+# the guest setup before the agent exists - nobody else is on it. The prohibition
+# stays either way (a crewmate that restarts its daemon mid-run still destroys its
+# own pipeline state), but the reason changes, and a rule whose stated reason is
+# false in context is a rule agents learn to discount.
+if [ "$VM" -eq 1 ]; then
+  RULE7='7. Never stop, restart, or update the `no-mistakes` daemon. In this microVM it is YOURS - the
+   guest setup started it before you existed and it dies with the VM - so restarting it does not
+   hurt other lanes, it destroys your own in-flight run and the gate state with it. On ANY
+   no-mistakes daemon error, append `blocked: {the daemon error}` and stop.'
+  # The VM is torn down when the run ends. A PR left open at CI-green would have
+  # nobody to merge it, so here the crewmate closes the loop itself - matching the
+  # captain'"'"'s methodology: he checks the result, not the merge.
+  NM_FINISH='After /no-mistakes reports CI green, merge the PR yourself with `gh`: squash merge and delete the branch.
+Tolerate a "already merged" / "not mergeable" response by re-reading the PR state before deciding it failed - a merge that already landed is success, not an error.
+Then append `done: PR {url} merged` and stop. You are finished.
+This differs from the host flow on purpose: the microVM is destroyed when your run ends, so a PR left at CI-green would have nobody to merge it.'
+else
+  RULE7='7. Never stop, restart, or update the shared `no-mistakes` daemon - it is one instance serving
+   every lane/home, so restarting it kills other lanes'"'"' in-flight pipeline runs. On ANY no-mistakes
+   daemon error, append `blocked: {the daemon error}` and stop; only firstmate manages the daemon.'
+  NM_FINISH='After /no-mistakes reports CI green (the CI-ready return point - do not wait for it to keep monitoring in the background until merge), append `done: PR {url} checks green` and stop. You are finished.'
+fi
+
 case "$MODE" in
   direct-PR)
     SETUP2=""
@@ -346,7 +380,7 @@ Two firstmate-specific rules layer on top of that guidance:
   When the decision comes back, feed it to the gate with \`no-mistakes axi respond\` and let the pipeline apply it - do not route the question to "the user" or implement the fix yourself.
 - Avoid \`--yes\`: it would silently bypass firstmate's authority check and any required captain escalation.
 
-After /no-mistakes reports CI green (the CI-ready return point - do not wait for it to keep monitoring in the background until merge), append \`done: PR {url} checks green\` and stop. You are finished.
+$NM_FINISH
 EOF
     ;;
 esac
@@ -394,9 +428,7 @@ $RULE1
 6. If a decision belongs above the implementation worker (product choices, destructive actions, ask-user findings),
    append \`needs-decision: {summary of options}\` and stop. Firstmate will apply the configured authority and reply with the decision.
    When firstmate replies or a blocker clears and you resume, append \`resolved: {how it was decided or unblocked}\` (add the same \`[key=<slug>]\` if you opened it with one) so the decision or blocker is durably closed and does not keep resurfacing.
-7. Never stop, restart, or update the shared \`no-mistakes\` daemon - it is one instance serving
-   every lane/home, so restarting it kills other lanes' in-flight pipeline runs. On ANY no-mistakes
-   daemon error, append \`blocked: {the daemon error}\` and stop; only firstmate manages the daemon.
+$RULE7
 
 # Project memory
 If \`AGENTS.md\` or \`CLAUDE.md\` already exists, or if this task produced durable project-intrinsic knowledge, run \`$FM_ROOT/bin/fm-ensure-agents-md.sh .\` in the worktree.
